---
import ArticleLayout from "../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";
---

<ArticleLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Image Identifier handles your images: browser-local checks, what may load over the network, and what we do not store."
>
  <span slot="crumb" class="text-fg">Privacy</span>

  <p>
    Image Identifier is designed so the image you select is analyzed in your browser. We do not
    upload your selected image bytes to an application backend for analysis, and we do not send them
    to a third-party detector API as part of the core tool.
  </p>

  <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The file you choose is read in the browser for the check.</li>
    <li>Results you see come from processing on your device for that session.</li>
    <li>We do not create accounts or store your images in a cloud gallery.</li>
    <li>We do not save image contents to localStorage by default.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What may use the network</h2>
  <p>
    “Runs in your browser” is not the same as “never uses the network.” The site may still request:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Static site assets (HTML, CSS, JavaScript, fonts, icons).</li>
    <li>Runtime files the tool needs to run (including WebAssembly and model files on first use).</li>
    <li>Analytics or ads only if they are enabled later — none are required for the tool today.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Those requests should not include your selected image bytes. See the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> for
    plain-language answers.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions: <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
